<h3>Custom themes</h3>
<p>
  By default, pk-gov pages use
  <code>--central-ministry-colour</code>
  as the accent colour. However, some pages may require different colours, such as certain ministry
  pages and pk-dev pages. In these situations, pages can have custom themes with the following
  snippet:
</p>
<pre>
&lt;style&gt;
  html {
    --theme: var(--colour-variable-here);
    --theme-accent: rgb(0, 0, 0);
    --theme-accent-alt: rgb(255, 255, 255);
  }
&lt;/style&gt;
</pre>
<p>Custom themes can be applied with the following steps:</p>
<ol>
  <li>
    The desired accent colour should be assigned to
    <code>--theme</code>.
  </li>
  <li>
    <code>--theme-accent</code>
    and
    <code>--theme-accent-alt</code>
    should be set based on the text contrast examples in the list of colour variables above. If
    black text is used,
    <code>--theme-accent</code>
    should be set to pure black (#000000) and
    <code>--theme-accent-alt</code>
    should be set to pure white (#FFFFFF), and vice versa for white text.
  </li>
</ol>
